#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
BRICK K.3 - Inline Study and Create integration.
Targets main.py (routing map plus one journey response field) and chat_test.html
(additive wrapper block only). Existing brick bodies are preserved exactly.
Prerequisites: BRICK K.2 in chat_test.html and BRICK K.1.5 in main.py.
Refuses BRICK K.3 in either file and refuses either existing backup.

Usage:
 python3 patch_brickK3.py --dry-run --dir /root/e5-ai-coach
 python3 patch_brickK3.py --dir /root/e5-ai-coach
Backups: main.py.bak-brickK3 and chat_test.html.bak-brickK3 (never overwritten).
Requires Node.js. No Python package installation or network access is required.
Runs Python compile, map/schema checks, full-inline node --check, unchanged K.2
regression suite and K.3 offline tests BEFORE creating backups or writing targets.
Each replacement is staged and fsynced. If the HTML replacement fails after the
backend replacement, main.py is restored atomically. Backups remain available.
This is not a cross-file transaction against process termination or power loss.
Rebuild the Docker image after apply when Dockerfile uses COPY . .:
 docker compose up -d --build
Rollback both files from their matching .bak-brickK3 backups, then rebuild.
"""
